{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>A mighty hunter before YHWH.</b> In the world — and likewise a great city of Elohim in all the world of HaShem there was no great city like it. Another interpretation: <b>before YHWH</b> — according to the spoken word, as in 'Cursed be the man before YHWH who rises and builds this city, Jericho,' and it is written: 'In his days Hi'el of Beth-El built Jericho, etc.' 'and in Segub his youngest son he set up its doors, according to the word of YHWH that He spoke through the hand of Joshua son of Nun.' From this you learn that 'before YHWH' means according to the spoken word; so too here it explains that from on High it was decreed upon Nimrod that a spirit of valorous strength would come upon him and he would seize victory wherever he goes." "<b>Therefore it is said, Like Nimrod.</b> Therefore, every man who arms his trainee to train him to grasp a sword blesses him with this blessing: 'Like Nimrod,' for HaShem decreed upon him to be a mighty hunter of the hunt, so that no beast of prey would slip from his hand — bear and forest boar and lion; so may you succeed with this sword that I gird upon you, and may you seize victory wherever you go.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:47.138625033Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}